+# Miller's relation in arbitrary characteristic
+
+The projective divisor `(P) + (Q) − (P+Q) − (O)` is principal on a smooth
+Weierstrass cubic in every characteristic. The chord and tangent
+factorization of the coordinate ideals gives the requisite divisor
+identities without restrictions on the values of `2` or `3` in the base
+field.
+
+These principal-divisor identities give the Abel–Jacobi description
+`Pic⁰(E) ≅ E`. The intermediate construction can also take the degree-zero
+property of principal divisors as an explicit hypothesis.
+
+Reference: Silverman, *The Arithmetic of Elliptic Curves*, III.3.4(e), p.63.
