+# Equality of places under multiplication
+
+For the multiplication isogeny `φ = [ℓ]` and a smooth point `P` with image `Q`,
+the comap of the point valuation at `P` under `φ*` is equivalent to the valuation
+at `Q`. If `Q` is affine this is its point valuation; if `Q = O`, it is the
+valuation at infinity.
+
+Equivalence means that the valuations have the same valuation ring:
+`[ℓ]* g` is regular at `P` exactly when `g` is regular at `Q`. The induced local
+homomorphism of discrete valuation rings has positive ramification index. This
+place identity only requires positivity; an order-one uniformizer pullback gives
+the additional unramified normalization.
+
+For affine `Q`, the division-polynomial coordinate formula determines residue
+matching, which extends to the function field through the local ring. At a torsion
+point `P`, kernel translation transports the coordinate orders `-2` and `-3` at
+infinity to the corresponding pullbacks at `P`.
+
+Reference: Silverman, *The Arithmetic of Elliptic Curves*, II.2.5–2.6 and III.4.10c.
 -/
 
