+`R = K(E)^q`. The Kähler differential of `[p]* x` vanishes, so it is a `p`-th
+power `g^p`. Since `K(E)/K(x)` is separable and `[p]* x ∈ K(x)`, the purely
+inseparable element `g` lies in `K(x)`. Induction gives
+`[q]* x ∈ K(x^q) ⊆ R`.
+
+The Weierstrass equation then makes `[q]* y` separable over `R`: the pulled-back
+quadratic has nonzero derivative at `[q]* y`, since `[q]*` is injective and
+`2y + a₁x + a₃ ≠ 0`. As `K(E)/R` is purely inseparable, `[q]* y` belongs to `R`.
+The argument applies in every characteristic.
 
