+# Separability and invariant differentials
+
+For an elliptic curve over a finite field of characteristic `p`, the
+pullback of the invariant differential by `m + n·π` has coefficient `m`.
+Thus separability is equivalent to `m ≠ 0` in the base field, or to
+`p ∤ m`. The coefficient calculations use additivity, the scalar formula,
+and vanishing of the Frobenius pullback.
