+# Frobenius base change and geometric witnesses over an algebraic closure
+
+For an elliptic curve over a finite field of cardinality `q = p ^ r`, the iterated relative
+`p`-Frobenius point map after base change agrees with geometric Frobenius: both send
+`(x, y)` to `(x ^ q, y ^ q)`. Heterogeneous equalities transport points across the curve
+equalities in the iterated construction.
+
+Consequently, the kernel of `1 − π` over the algebraic closure is the finite image of the
+rational points, and its cardinality is the rational point count. A supplied degree identity
+identifies this cardinality with the isogeny degree. A dual composition `φ ∘ δ = [N]`, with
+`N` nonzero in the algebraic closure, gives surjectivity through surjectivity of multiplication
+by `N`. These facts construct the scaling data from the two dual composition identities,
+divisor-pullback functoriality, translation covariance, and the degree identity.
+
+The geometric ingredients correspond to Silverman, *The Arithmetic of Elliptic Curves*,
+III.4.10, III.6.2(a), III.8.2, III.8.6.1, and V.1.1–3.
