+
+For the isogenies `1 − π` and `rπ − s` over an algebraic closure of a finite field,
+generic-point translation covariance implies covariance of every function-field element.
+Its restriction to kernel translations supplies the invariance used in the Galois
+calculation of the kernel cardinality. Separability, normality and a translation-torsor
+condition identify this cardinality with the isogeny degree. Surjectivity follows from
+a supplied dual composition and surjectivity of multiplication by a nonzero integer.
+
+References: Silverman, *The Arithmetic of Elliptic Curves*, III.4.10, III.5.5,
